  "domain": "blockchain",
  "definition": "Uniswap is a decentralised exchange (DEX) protocol deployed on Ethereum that enables permissionless, non-custodial token swaps through an Automated Market Maker (AMM) mechanism. Rather than maintaining an order book, it uses liquidity pools governed by the constant-product invariant (x \u00d7 y = k), where liquidity providers deposit token pairs and earn fees proportional to their pool share. Successive protocol versions have introduced concentrated liquidity (v3) and multi-hop routing, making Uniswap a foundational primitive of decentralised finance.",
